  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ffd2926e-2892-54a4-91fd-e017ecb8d869" activityNameId="6ae7a355-57f4-541d-8007-23199e9e2e96" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Open cast mine, lignite</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Open cast mine, lignite
Information was available only for a few mines. For the preparation of this module only amounts per tonne were available. The module has to be considered as a first approximation and may not reflect specific mines. Lifetime is assumed to be 30 years to take into account the lifetime of machinery. No information was available that could allow a direct estimation of the average annual production of lignite mines in Europe. Therefore the total lifetime production of 100 million tonne for the model lignite mine has been extrapolated from the value assumed for the model hard coal mine taking into account the difference between the low heating values. Therefore this total lifetime production shall be considered as a normalisation factor more than an actual average value for the real mines. No explosives are necessary for open up the mine. Mostly mobile installations are used.;
UUID: 1546cd6a-943c-3326-9867-cfa4633b8b16
This module includes an estimation of the most important construction materials and energy use for the mine. The machinery used for mining operation has been included in this module, because the relevant material use is not separated from the total material use in the available references. Land use for the infrastructure is not included, because due to lack of information it cannot be seperated from the land use during the operation of the mine.
Location: Average data from Austria, Germany and Russian Federation.
Technology: Average technology of the time period considered.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_1546cd6a-943c-3326-9867-cfa4633b8b16.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
